From a9439cf2c097215314a7bf37e3134e0178e3a42f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iced-Cream <86374804+Iced-Cream@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:56:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Mod storage: a field's "offset" pins it to its bits

A storage field in mod.json can take "offset": N, its first bit in the scope. The allocator
places it there in every lockfile, the first build's too, so a mod moving data an older build of
its own kept in these bytes reads the same bits under both builds (elekloader issue #423: a sound
field at bit 30 and one at bit 42 land on stored +0x78..+0x7b). A hand-written lockfile can't do
this: each user's build keeps its own.

- store.allocate takes pins; a repack places the pinned fields at their offsets and packs the
  others around them, each at the lowest bits clear (mod, sym order; widest first where that
  leaves one out), so another mod's new field no longer moves a pin. Without pins the order and
  the bits are the ones it has always packed (the existing store vectors are unchanged).
- A new field may take the gaps pins leave below "next": those bits never held anything. A pin
  on another field's bits, or on a freed field's, repacks the scope.
- A field whose offset changes moves there, its data dropped ("moved to its offset").
- Refused: two pinned fields on one bit; a pin that ends past the scope's room with the build's
  core (core's own bytes lie past it), naming the core that has the room; fields that don't fit
  around their pins. "offset" must be a whole number, 0 or more.
- +Drive mods can't pin a field: the boot linker already refuses "offset" as a format error
  (now tested, C and twin).
- js/: the same in store.ts and link.ts; store-vectors.json gains pin_runs and offset decls.
- docs/FORMAT.md and docs/ADAPTING.md ("Mod storage (core-ar2 0.2, Analog Rytm MKII)").

The lockfile format doesn't change: a pin is not stored, a field keeps its place while its place
is its offset. An older elekloader refuses a mod.json with "offset" (an unknown storage key).
