- "description": "The boot copier, the hook bus, mod storage and parameter pages for the Analog Rytm MKII: every other mod needs it. The Digitakt mk1's core.s, settings.s and render.s with the Rytm's addresses, and store.c: fields mods declare, placed by elekloader from the build's lockfile and kept in bytes stock never uses or always holds at 0; and pages.s: parameter pages and parameter overrides mods add through the tables core_pages and core_params (and core_page_fns, a page whose knobs follow the sound), from the first instructions of the four routines a page goes through, and the page keys' lists, stock's pages and then the ones mods add through core_view_pages, which the page key steps through (skipping a page while its mod says it is hidden, with the page's title in the header), and which keeps its page when the view is shown again; load.s: the audio interrupt's load, core_audio_load, for mods with work they can skip; and machines.c: machines mods add in the hidden slots 34..43 through core_machines, written into the machine table and the slots' parameter records at boot; and lock.c and lock.s (0.8): lockable parameters, sound fields with lock codes from the lockfile that mods register in core_lock_params, listed as LFO destinations (core_lfo_offset) and taken by RANDOMIZE PAGE and RELOAD PAGE; and rows.c and rows.s (0.8): their p-locks, as lock rows with their codes in each pattern's row pool, set with a trig held and read by mods while the trig plays (core_lock_value); and scenes.c and scenes.s (0.8): their scene locks and performance depths, as entries with their codes in each kit's lists, set with a pad held in scene or performance edit and read by mods (core_scene_value, core_perf_offset). And midi.c and midi.s (0.8): their NRPNs (MSB 4, LSB the code - 42) and, for the first 33 codes, CCs from the 33 stock leaves unused, taken in on a track's channel and sent when a mod's knob turns one. On its own it changes nothing the unit does. And smooth.c (0.9): the value stock would play for a lockable parameter (core_param_value), its target (the sound, a p-lock, a scene lock) smoothed with stock's one-pole and the performances and the LFO added after, computed only when a mod reads it; a field declared \"smooth\": false jumps. And routes.c and routes.s (0.9): a lockable parameter declared \"mod\": true as a destination in each sound's VELOCITY MOD and AFTERTOUCH lists, the route keeping its code in its own byte, shown on its knob, taken out of stock's apply and handed to the mod (core_mod_offset), and added in core_param_value. And the FX track (0.9): a lockable kit field is the FX track's parameter, an FX LFO destination (core_fx_lfo_dst keeps its code), p-locked, locked in scenes and performances and on MIDI on the FX track, read with track 12; and a code an LFO points to no longer reaches the stored sound or kit through stock's edit write (st_sound_through, st_fx_through). And finish.s (0.7): an OS upgrade's restart sends the panel link's and the UART's queued bytes before it masks interrupts, where stock can hang on SUCCESS! REBOOTING. And ev_project_save (0.10): f(pre, how) before and after every whole save of the live project to a +Drive slot (SAVE PROJECT, SAVE PROJECT AS, the project menu's saves, an empty slot's LOAD), with the kind of save and the slot; a field set before the save is in the saved copy. And (0.10) core_param_value at about a quarter of 0.9's cost, and core_param_handle and core_param_value_h to read by a handle. And (0.11) p-locks a mod keeps itself: a knob id from 555 in a core_param_locks entry gets stock's lock calls with the track and step, its label and name, live recording's step, and core_held_step for its text. And (0.11) step tags: a mod's 16-bit handle on each step of each pattern (core_step_owners, core_step_tag, core_step_tag_set, core_step_tags), kept in RAM and moved wherever stock moves the step, with ev_steps telling the mod what moved, dropped, reloaded or changed length. And (0.11) the moments: ev_sysex_in (a SysEx message in, which a mod may take), core_midi_try_send (USB MIDI out that never waits), the UI's current kit, track and pattern with their items, ev_kit (a kit selected or pushed to the engine; a stopped kit change drops the playing trig's mod locks), the live project's name, \"handle\": true storage fields walked by core_handle_fields, and ev_project_slot (a +Drive slot cleared, initialized or pasted outside a save). And (0.11) the sequencer: ev_seq_step (the tracks that reached a step this tick and those whose next step trigs, from the clock, with the first step after PLAY seeded), ev_seq_tick (each clock tick), ev_transport (the play state changed), and core_transport, core_pattern_now, core_pattern_next, core_tempo, core_track_speed and core_track_step. And (0.12) room for +Drive mods: spare entries in its tables for the Drive Loader to fill at boot, \"max\": 8 on core_step_owners, and the render events marked as such. And (0.13, screen.c) the screen calls: text in stock's 17 fonts by stock's own text routine, a key event handed to stock alone (core_stock_key), whether a stock overlay or window is up (core_stock_overlay), the TRK LEVEL readout's window and header field, and stock's progress box. And (0.13) knob looks: a mod's own knob id takes the look of any stock knob (its UI record and its range) or a UI record of the mod's own, through core_knob_looks, where stock drew record 0's dial. And (0.14) +Drive storage: ev_boot_drive (once at boot, at 0x401009e0 in main(), with the +Drive mounted and the working project loaded, before audio and the UI start), where the Drive Loader may set the live layout in core_store_ids and core_store_gens, and the LFO destinations' fields in core_lfo_dsts for +Drive \"lfo\" fields; the boot's project load is finished after it, loading the working project again when the layout moved, so ev_project(1) at boot comes after the +Drive mods are linked. And (0.15, drive.c) mod folders in the +Drive browser: a mod's folder after the root's entries in SAMPLES and the slot browser through core_drive_folders, its listing asked without waiting and read again when the mod calls core_drive_refill, kept read-only by core's guards on stock's filesystem calls. And (0.15) stock knob faces: a stock id's label, name, look and range per sound, through core_knob_faces, for a framework mod whose machine takes over stock records. And (0.15, pads.c) ev_pad: a pad's strike, release and pressure before stock plays the pad or selects its track, which a mod may take; and ev_leds with core_led: pad and key LED colours a mod sets each frame, shown over stock's and given back when it stops. And (0.15, voiceio.c) a voice's note end for its machine's engine (core_voice_released), the track mutes (core_track_mutes, core_set_track_mutes) and DIN MIDI out that never waits (core_midi_din_try_send). And (0.15, usbin.s) the USB input's gain: one mod at a time holds one of stock's four USB TO MAIN [dB] steps in place of the setting (core_usb_in_gain), which stays as it was. And (0.16) the silent-voice skip (idle.c, idle.s; analog-rytm-mk2/voice.h), off at boot and on while a mod asks for it (core_voice_skip_want) and none holds it off (core_voice_skip_hold): a voice slot's machine routine, which stock calls every block forever once the slot has played, is not called while the slot is silent and the call changes nothing sent to the voices, and at its next SYN trig the slot's digital state goes back to its power-on values, so that note starts like the first one after a power-on (this changes sound slightly). And (0.16) the sample-layer skip (sample.s; analog-rytm-mk2/voice.h), off at boot and on while a mod asks for it (core_sample_skip_want) and none holds it off (core_voice_skip_hold): a voice slot whose sample layer is not playing and whose filter history is zero no longer runs its resample, filter and output stage, which stock runs every block on zeros; the sound is unchanged, bit for bit. And (0.16) the UI skip (cast.s; analog-rytm-mk2/ui.h), off at boot and on while a mod asks for it (core_ui_skip_want) and none holds it off (core_ui_skip_hold): stock's __dynamic_cast keeps its answers in a small memo keyed by the source's vtable pointer, the two types and the hint, so the main screen's twenty \"is this view open?\" scans per refresh stop walking the class tree; the answers are always stock's. And (0.16) the FX skip (fx.c, fx.s; analog-rytm-mk2/fx.h), off at boot: with core_fx_skip_want on and no core_fx_skip_hold, the send loop leaves out voice slots that send nothing and the delay is not called while nothing feeds it and its line holds only zeros (both exact); with core_reverb_clear_want on too, a reverb whose input has been 0 for 1 s and whose output is below 1 LSB of 24 bits is cleared and then not called until its input moves (this changes sound slightly). And (0.16) submenus: a SETTINGS row a mod adds opens a menu of its own rows, stock's checkbox menu view (submenu.s; analog-rytm-mk2/settings.h, core_submenu_open). And (0.17, std.c) the standard events (std1): a mod with \"events\": \"std1\" subscribes to ev_boot, ev_tick, ev_draw, ev_key, ev_enc, ev_settings, ev_project, ev_render_in, ev_param_turn, ev_sysex_in and ev_seq_tick through core's \"std\" map, with core_redraw, core_post, core_timer, core_setting_add and the draw helpers (std1.h; analog-rytm-mk2/keys.h, params.h, ports.h); and at new sites the UI and system events ev_boot_done, ev_idle, ev_crash, ev_usb, ev_key_leds (core_led_set), ev_mode, ev_param_set, ev_clip, ev_pattern, ev_mute and ev_view (ui.c, ui.s; analog-rytm-mk2/ui.h, leds.h); and at new sites the MIDI events ev_midi_in, ev_midi_cc, ev_midi_pc, ev_midi_out and ev_seq_midi (stdmidi.c, stdmidi.s; analog-rytm-mk2/ports.h); and in the audio interrupt's trig intake ev_voice_start and ev_voice_end (stdvoice.c, stdvoice.s). And (0.17, flags.c, flags.s) knob flags: a mod's own knob id opens a destination list when turned or pushed, as LFO DEST does, through core_knob_flags, where stock read record 0's flags. And (0.18, restart.s) core_restart, a reboot from a task once the +Drive is idle and the panel link and UART have sent what they hold, core_restart_now, and core_project_keep, the working project written from the live project before such a reboot (analog-rytm-mk2/system.h). And (0.19, usbring.c, usbring.s) the USB-MIDI sender's early wrap: a call of more than 0x2f bytes with the ring's index above 0xfbf waits until nothing is unsent before stock skips the ring's tail, where stock waited less and could overwrite events not yet sent (large SysEx replies, such as /mods reads in 8 KB chunks, reached the host with one event damaged); core_midi_try_send's room test follows the same rule.",
